IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg1-s103-filing`
IMPORT `dg1-s101-formation`
IMPORT `dg1-s102a-required-contents`
IMPORT `dg1-s111-s115-jurisdiction-and-forum`
IMPORT `dg1-s102b-optional-provisions`
IMPORT `dg1-s102e-name-reservation`
IMPORT `dg1-s108-organization`
IMPORT `dg1-s109-bylaws-and-emergency-powers`
IMPORT `dg1-s114-nonstock`
IMPORT `dg1-s116-documents`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 101 to 116 (piece dg1) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation
-- Law: an incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder. The questions are
-- the ones that person asks: what the Law lets them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the
-- corporation, and what can be done to them.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, a number, a date, or one of the modules' own choices,
-- each named in the text's words) with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1
-- modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is
-- then called; no rule is restated here. Records are built with named fields (WITH), each field bound to the one
-- input that states it. The cases in dg1-cases-seat.l4 call the questions with the inputs in the order written
-- above each question; a binding to the wrong input is seen only if some case gives the two inputs different
-- values (NOTES, Before this is worth relying on).
--
-- OFFICIALS. The Secretary of State, the Division of Corporations and the Court of Chancery have no seat. What they
-- must do, or may do, appears as what the person is owed or exposed to; a finding or waiver the Law leaves to them is
-- asked as a fact ("Has the Division of Corporations waived ...?"), never guessed.
--
-- A QUESTION THAT ANSWERS "NOT COVERED". Where the text does not decide, the answer is a MAYBE: NOTHING means "the
-- Law does not say" (for example, 101(a) for a limited liability company), and is never turned into yes or no.
--
-- What this layer does not ask: the figures that section 391 (dg11) and chapter 5 set (fees, total assets) are asked
-- as numbers; the time of day within a date is not carried (a question that turns on it answers NOTHING).

§ `Delaware General Corporation Law, sections 101 to 116 -- the questions of someone who incorporates, directs or holds stock`

§§ `Forming the corporation (sections 101 to 107)`

-- s 101(a). "Any person, partnership, association or corporation, singly or jointly with others, and without regard
-- to such person's or entity's residence, domicile or state of incorporation, may incorporate or organize a
-- corporation under this chapter" by filing a certificate of incorporation. The Law does not say whether a limited
-- liability company, statutory trust, real estate investment trust or common-law trust is one of those.
@export May I (or the entity I act for) incorporate a Delaware corporation (s 101(a))?
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `Kind of entity` @desc What are you (or the entity you act for)? A corporation is chosen with its kind, for example a stock corporation.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I incorporate a Delaware corporation` IS
    `s 101(a) the entity may incorporate or organize a corporation under this chapter` `what I am`

-- s 101(b)
@export May the corporation be formed for this business or these purposes (s 101(b))?
GIVEN `the business or purposes are lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the business or purposes lawful?
      `the Constitution or other law of this State otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Constitution or another law of Delaware prohibit this business or these purposes for a corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation be formed for this business or these purposes` IF
    `s 101(b) a corporation may be incorporated to conduct or promote the business or purposes` `the business or purposes are lawful` `the Constitution or other law of this State otherwise provides`

-- s 101(c). A public utility may be organized under the chapter; one that operates within the State is subject also to
-- the special provisions of Title 26.
@export Is my public utility corporation also subject to the special provisions of Title 26 (s 101(c))?
GIVEN `my corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities?
      `the public utilities are within this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the public utilities within Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my public utility corporation also subject to Title 26` IF
    `s 101(c) the corporation is subject also to the special provisions and requirements of Title 26` `my corporation is for constructing, maintaining and operating public utilities` `the public utilities are within this State`

-- s 104. "Certificate of incorporation" includes the later certificates, agreements of merger or consolidation, plans
-- of reorganization and other instruments filed under the title that amend or supplement it.
@export Does this instrument count as part of my corporation's certificate of incorporation (s 104)?
GIVEN `it is the original certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the original certificate of incorporation filed to create the corporation?
      `it was filed under a section of the Delaware General Corporation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it filed pursuant to a section of Title 8 (for example a certificate of amendment, an agreement of merger or a plan of reorganization)?
      `it amends or supplements the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have the effect of amending or supplementing the corporation's certificate of incorporation in some respect?
      `the context requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context of the section you are reading require that "certificate of incorporation" mean only the original certificate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this instrument count as part of my corporation's certificate of incorporation` IF
    `s 104 the instrument is part of the certificate of incorporation` `it is the original certificate of incorporation` `it was filed under a section of the Delaware General Corporation Law` `it amends or supplements the certificate of incorporation` `the context requires otherwise`

-- s 105. A copy certified by the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of three kinds of matter.
@export Will a certified copy of the certificate be received as prima facie evidence of this matter (s 105)?
GIVEN `the copy has been certified by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State duly certified the copy?
      `the certificate was filed in the Secretary of State's office as the title requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate (or restated certificate, or other certificate) filed in the Secretary of State's office as a provision of Title 8 requires?
      `the matter` IS A `s 105 Matter evidenced` @desc What do you want to prove with it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a certified copy be received as prima facie evidence of this matter` IS
    `s 105 the certified copy is received as prima facie evidence of the matter` `the copy has been certified by the Secretary of State` `the certificate was filed in the Secretary of State's office as the title requires` `the matter`

-- s 106. From the date of filing (or a later effective date under s 103(d)) the incorporators who signed the
-- certificate are a body corporate by the name in the certificate.
@export From what date does my corporation exist as a body corporate (s 106)?
GIVEN `my certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of incorporation executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103?
      `the date my certificate was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate of incorporation filed with the Secretary of State?
      `my certificate names a later effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say it takes effect at a later date than the filing date?
      `the later effective date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Any date if it does not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `From what date does my corporation exist` IS
    `s 106 the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate` `my certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` `the date my certificate was filed` `my later date`
    WHERE
        `my later date` MEANS IF `my certificate names a later effective date` THEN JUST `the later effective date` ELSE NOTHING

@export Does my corporation exist on this day (s 106)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `my certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate of incorporation executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103?
      `the date my certificate was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate of incorporation filed with the Secretary of State?
      `my certificate names a later effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate say it takes effect at a later date than the filing date?
      `the later effective date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Any date if it does not.)
      `the corporation has been dissolved or its existence otherwise terminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been dissolved, or its existence otherwise terminated as the Law provides?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation exist on this day` IF
    `s 106 the body corporate exists on the day` `the day` `my start` `the corporation has been dissolved or its existence otherwise terminated`
    WHERE
        `my start` MEANS `s 106 the date from which the incorporators are a body corporate` `my certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103` `the date my certificate was filed` `my later date`
        `my later date` MEANS IF `my certificate names a later effective date` THEN JUST `the later effective date` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 107. If the first directors were not named in the certificate, the incorporators manage the affairs of the
-- corporation until the directors are elected, and may do whatever is necessary and proper to perfect the organization.
@export As an incorporator, do I manage the corporation's affairs now (s 107)?
GIVEN `the first directors were named in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting?
      `the directors have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors been elected?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As an incorporator, do I manage the corporation's affairs now` IF
    `s 107 the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation` `the first directors were named in the certificate` `the directors have been elected`

@export As an incorporator, may I do this act (s 107)?
GIVEN `the first directors were named in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting?
      `the directors have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors been elected?
      `the act` IS A `s 107 Act of the incorporators` @desc What do you want to do?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As an incorporator, may I do this act` IS
    `s 107 the incorporators may do the act` (`s 107 the incorporators manage the affairs of the corporation` `the first directors were named in the certificate` `the directors have been elected`) `the act`

§§ `What the certificate of incorporation must set forth (section 102(a))`

-- s 102(a)(1)(i). The name shall contain one of twelve words (or an abbreviation, or a word of like import of a
-- foreign country in roman characters), unless the Division of Corporations waives that on a certificate of total
-- assets of at least $10,000,000 or, in its sole discretion, for a nonprofit nonstock association of professionals.
@export Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires, or has the Division of Corporations waived the requirement (s 102(a)(1)(i))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? (A stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; or a charitable nonstock corporation.)
      `my name has a listed word` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain one of the words association, company, corporation, club, foundation, fund, incorporated, institute, society, union, syndicate or limited, or an abbreviation of one, with or without punctuation?
      `my name has a word of like import` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain a word (or abbreviation) of like import of a foreign country or jurisdiction, written in roman characters or letters?
      `we filed a certificate of total assets` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation execute, acknowledge and file with the Secretary of State a certificate stating its total assets?
      `the total assets we stated` IS A NUMBER @desc What total assets does that certificate state (as defined in section 503(i) of Title 8), in dollars? (0 if none was filed.)
      `the Division thinks my name looks like a person's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Division of Corporations determined that the name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person?
      `we are an association of professionals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an association of professionals?
      `the Division has waived it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Division of Corporations waived the requirement for this name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation's name contain a word the Law requires` IF
    `s 102(a)(1)(i) the name satisfies the requirement as to words` `my name facts` `my kind of corporation`
    WHERE
        `my name facts` MEANS `s 102(a)(1)(i) Name words` WITH
            `the name contains one of the listed words or an abbreviation of one, with or without punctuation` IS `my name has a listed word`
            `the name contains words of like import of foreign countries or jurisdictions, written in roman characters or letters` IS `my name has a word of like import`
            `the corporation executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 a certificate stating its total assets` IS `we filed a certificate of total assets`
            `the total assets the certificate states, as defined in § 503(i) of this title, in dollars` IS `the total assets we stated`
            `the Division determines that the name is, or might otherwise appear to be, that of a natural person` IS `the Division thinks my name looks like a person's`
            `the corporation is an association of professionals` IS `we are an association of professionals`
            `the Division of Corporations waives the requirement` IS `the Division has waived it`

-- s 102(a)(1)(ii)
@export Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the Division's records from reserved names and from other entities' names (s 102(a)(1)(ii))?
GIVEN `my name is distinguishable on the records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name such as to distinguish it upon the records in the office of the Division of Corporations from the reserved names and from the names of each other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company, registered series or statutory trust organized or registered under the laws of this State?
      `I have written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who reserved the name (or the other entity) give written consent, executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State?
      `the Division has waived distinction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Division of Corporations waived the requirement?
      `we showed substantial use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown to the Secretary of State's satisfaction that the corporation or a predecessor entity previously made substantial use of the name or a substantially similar name?
      `we showed reasonable efforts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown to the Secretary of State's satisfaction that you made reasonable efforts to secure the written consent?
      `we showed the waiver serves the State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you shown to the Secretary of State's satisfaction that the waiver is in the interest of the State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's name distinguishable on the records` IF
    `s 102(a)(1)(ii) the name satisfies the requirement as to distinction on the records` `my name distinction`
    WHERE
        `my name distinction` MEANS `s 102(a)(1)(ii) Name distinct` WITH
            `the name is such as to distinguish it upon the records in the office of the Division of Corporations from the reserved names and from the names of each other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company, registered series or statutory trust organized or registered under the laws of this State` IS `my name is distinguishable on the records`
            `the person who has reserved the name, or the other foreign corporation or domestic or foreign entity, gave written consent executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103` IS `I have written consent`
            `the Division of Corporations waives the requirement` IS `the Division has waived distinction`
            `the corporation demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary of State that it or a predecessor entity previously has made substantial use of the name or a substantially similar name` IS `we showed substantial use`
            `the corporation demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary of State that it has made reasonable efforts to secure the written consent` IS `we showed reasonable efforts`
            `the corporation demonstrates to the satisfaction of the Secretary of State that the waiver is in the interest of the State` IS `we showed the waiver serves the State`

-- s 102(a)(1)(iii)
@export May my corporation's name contain the word "trust" (s 102(a)(1)(iii))?
GIVEN `my name contains the word trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain the word "trust"?
      `section 395 permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 395 of Title 8 permit the use of the word "trust" in the name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation's name contain the word trust` IF
    `s 102(a)(1)(iii) the name satisfies the requirement as to the word trust` `my name contains the word trust` `section 395 permits it`

-- s 102(a)(1)(iv)
@export May my corporation's name contain the word "bank" (s 102(a)(1)(iv))?
GIVEN `my name contains bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name contain the word "bank" or a variation of it?
      `we are a bank supervised in this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name the name of a bank reporting to and under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State?
      `we are a subsidiary of a bank` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name the name of a subsidiary of a bank or savings association (as defined in the Federal Deposit Insurance Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1813)?
      `we are a regulated holding company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 or the Home Owners' Loan Act?
      `the Division finds the context is not banking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Division of Corporations determined that the word is used in a context clearly not purporting to refer to a banking business?
      `the Division finds no risk of misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Division determined that the use is not otherwise likely to mislead the public about the nature of the business, or to lead to a pattern and practice of abuse that might cause harm to the public or the State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation's name contain the word bank` IF
    `s 102(a)(1)(iv) the name satisfies the requirement as to the word bank` `my name and bank`
    WHERE
        `my name and bank` MEANS `s 102(a)(1)(iv) Name bank` WITH
            `the name contains the word bank or a variation of it` IS `my name contains bank`
            `the name is the name of a bank reporting to and under the supervision of the State Bank Commissioner of this State` IS `we are a bank supervised in this State`
            `the name is the name of a subsidiary of a bank or savings association, as those terms are defined in the Federal Deposit Insurance Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1813` IS `we are a subsidiary of a bank`
            `the corporation is regulated under the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956, 12 U.S.C. § 1841 et seq., or the Home Owners' Loan Act, 12 U.S.C. § 1461 et seq.` IS `we are a regulated holding company`
            `the Division determines that the word is used in a context clearly not purporting to refer to a banking business` IS `the Division finds the context is not banking`
            `the Division determines that the use is not otherwise likely to mislead the public about the nature of the business of the corporation or to lead to a pattern and practice of abuse that might cause harm to the interests of the public or the State` IS `the Division finds no risk of misleading`

-- s 102(a)(2)
@export Does the certificate state the registered office and registered agent as required (s 102(a)(2))?
GIVEN `it states the registered office address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the address of the corporation's registered office in this State?
      `the address is stated as section 131(c) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that address stated in accordance with section 131(c) of Title 8?
      `it states the registered agent's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name of the corporation's registered agent at that address?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate state the registered office and registered agent as required` IF
    `s 102(a)(2) the certificate sets forth the registered office and registered agent` `my registered office and agent`
    WHERE
        `my registered office and agent` MEANS `s 102(a)(2) Registered office and agent stated` WITH
            `the certificate states the address of the corporation's registered office in this State` IS `it states the registered office address`
            `that address is stated in accordance with § 131(c)` IS `the address is stated as section 131(c) requires`
            `the certificate states the name of the corporation's registered agent at that address` IS `it states the registered agent's name`

-- s 102(a)(3)
@export Is the certificate's statement of the corporation's purposes enough (s 102(a)(3))?
GIVEN `it states the purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the nature of the business or purposes to be conducted or promoted?
      `it states the general purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the certificate's statement of the corporation's purposes enough` IF
    `s 102(a)(3) the certificate sets forth the nature of the business or purposes` `it states the purposes` `it states the general purpose`

@export Is this act or activity within my corporation's purposes (s 102(a)(3))?
GIVEN `the certificate states the general purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the purpose of the corporation is to engage in any lawful act or activity for which corporations may be organized under the General Corporation Law of Delaware?
      `the act is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or activity lawful?
      `the certificate expressly excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate contain an express limitation that excludes the act or activity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this act or activity within my corporation's purposes` IS
    `s 102(a)(3) the act or activity is within the purposes of the corporation` `the certificate states the general purpose` `the act is lawful` `the certificate expressly excludes it`

-- s 102(a)(4), a corporation that may issue stock. The statements of rights and of the board's authority are needed
-- only to the extent the incorporators desire them.
@export Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the number of classes of stock` IS A NUMBER @desc How many classes of stock is the corporation to be authorized to issue?
      `it states the total number of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the total number of shares of stock the corporation has authority to issue?
      `it states par value or no par` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is one class: does it state the par value of each share, or that all shares are without par value?
      `it states the number of each class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is more than one class: does it state the number of shares of each class?
      `it states which classes have par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there is more than one class: does it specify each class without par value, each class with par value, and the par value of each of those?
      `we want to fix rights in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the incorporators want the certificate itself to fix the designations, powers, preferences, rights, qualifications, limitations or restrictions (section 151) of any class or series?
      `it states them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the certificate set out a statement of them?
      `we want the board to fix some by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the incorporators want to grant the board of directors authority to fix by resolution any of them that the certificate does not fix?
      `it grants that authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the certificate expressly grant that authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate state my corporation's authorized stock as required` IS
    `s 102(a)(4) the certificate sets forth the authorized stock` `my authorized stock`
    WHERE
        `my authorized stock` MEANS `s 102(a)(4) Authorized stock stated` WITH
            `the number of classes of stock the corporation is to be authorized to issue` IS `the number of classes of stock`
            `the certificate states the total number of shares of stock which the corporation has authority to issue` IS `it states the total number of shares`
            `the certificate states the par value of each of the shares, or that all the shares are to be without par value` IS `it states par value or no par`
            `the certificate states the number of shares of each class` IS `it states the number of each class`
            `the certificate specifies each class the shares of which are to be without par value, each class the shares of which are to have par value, and the par value of the shares of each class with par value` IS `it states which classes have par value`
            `the incorporators desire to fix by the certificate the designations, powers, preferences and rights, and qualifications, limitations or restrictions, permitted by § 151 for a class or series` IS `we want to fix rights in the certificate`
            `the certificate sets forth a statement of them` IS `it states them`
            `the incorporators desire to grant the board of directors authority to fix by resolution any of them not fixed by the certificate` IS `we want the board to fix some by resolution`
            `the certificate sets forth an express grant of that authority` IS `it grants that authority`

-- s 102(a)(4), a nonstock corporation.
@export Does the certificate (or the bylaws) state what my nonstock corporation must state (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the certificate says no capital stock may be issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the corporation is not authorized to issue capital stock?
      `the certificate or bylaws say who the members are` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate state what my nonstock corporation must state` IF
    `s 102(a)(4) the certificate and the bylaws set forth what a nonstock corporation must state` `my nonstock statements`
    WHERE
        `my nonstock statements` MEANS `s 102(a)(4) Nonstock corporation stated` WITH
            `the certificate states that the corporation is not authorized to issue capital stock` IS `the certificate says no capital stock may be issued`
            `the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members` IS `the certificate or bylaws say who the members are`

@export Am I a member of this nonstock corporation (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the certificate or bylaws state who the members are` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate or the bylaws state the conditions of membership, or other criteria for identifying members?
      `I meet those conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the stated conditions or criteria?
      `I may vote for the governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body under the certificate, the bylaws or otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a member of this nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 102(a)(4) the person is a member of the nonstock corporation` `the certificate or bylaws state who the members are` `I meet those conditions` `I may vote for the governing body`

@export May my nonstock corporation make this provision for its members (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `the provision` IS A `s 102(a)(4) Provision for members` @desc What does the provision do?
      `the chapter provides otherwise for voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a voting provision: does the Delaware General Corporation Law elsewhere provide otherwise?
      `it is in the certificate or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision set forth in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my nonstock corporation make this provision for its members` IF
    `s 102(a)(4) the nonstock corporation may make the provision for its members` `my kind of corporation` `the provision` `the chapter provides otherwise for voting` `it is in the certificate or bylaws`

@export Is an act of my nonstock corporation still valid although the corporation has no members (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVEN `the corporate act is otherwise valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporate act otherwise valid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an act of my nonstock corporation still valid although it has no members` IF
    `s 102(a)(4) the corporate act remains valid although the nonstock corporation has no members` `the corporate act is otherwise valid`

@export Is my nonstock corporation forfeited or dissolved because it has no members (s 102(a)(4))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nonstock corporation forfeited or dissolved because it has no members` IF
    `s 102(a)(4) the nonstock corporation has forfeited its existence or is dissolved because it has no members`

-- s 102(a)(5), (6)
@export Must the certificate name the first directors (s 102(a)(6))?
GIVEN `the incorporators' powers end on filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the powers of the incorporators to terminate upon the filing of the certificate of incorporation?
      `it names them with mailing addresses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the names and mailing addresses of the persons who are to serve as directors until the first annual meeting or until their successors are elected and qualify?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate name the first directors as the Law requires` IF
    `s 102(a)(6) the certificate sets forth the first directors` `the incorporators' powers end on filing` `it names them with mailing addresses`

@export Does the certificate name the incorporators (s 102(a)(5))?
GIVEN `it names each incorporator with a mailing address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the name and mailing address of each incorporator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the certificate name the incorporators` IF
    `s 102(a)(5) the certificate sets forth the incorporators` `it names each incorporator with a mailing address`

§§ `What the certificate of incorporation may also contain (section 102(b), (c), (d) and (f))`

-- s 102(b)(1)
@export May the certificate of incorporation contain this provision (s 102(b)(1))?
GIVEN `it is about management, or the powers of the corporation, directors or stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision for the management of the business or the conduct of the affairs of the corporation, or does it create, define, limit or regulate the powers of the corporation, the directors, the stockholders (or any class of them), or the governing body or members of a nonstock corporation?
      `it is contrary to the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision contrary to the laws of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 102(b)(1), may the certificate of incorporation contain this provision` IF
    `s 102(b)(1) the certificate of incorporation may contain the provision` `it is about management, or the powers of the corporation, directors or stockholders` `it is contrary to the laws of this State`

@export Must the certificate of incorporation contain any of the optional matters listed in section 102(b) (s 102(b))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the certificate of incorporation contain any of the optional matters` IF
    `s 102(b) the certificate of incorporation is required to contain the matter listed in subsection (b)`

@export May a provision the Law lets the bylaws contain be put in the certificate of incorporation instead (s 102(b)(1))?
GIVEN `a section of the Law lets the bylaws contain it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a section of the Delaware General Corporation Law require or permit the provision to be stated in the bylaws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a provision the Law lets the bylaws contain be put in the certificate instead` IF
    `s 102(b)(1) a provision that this chapter requires or permits to be stated in the bylaws may instead be stated in the certificate of incorporation` `a section of the Law lets the bylaws contain it`

-- s 102(b)(2). The compromise or arrangement provision, in haec verba.
@export Has the certificate set out the compromise or arrangement provision in the Law's own words (s 102(b)(2))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `it uses the words of paragraph (b)(2)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set forth the provision in the very words of paragraph (b)(2)(i) (the form for a corporation other than a nonstock corporation)?
      `it uses the words of paragraph (b)(2)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set forth the provision in the very words of paragraph (b)(2)(ii) (the form for a nonstock corporation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the certificate set out the compromise or arrangement provision in the Law's own words` IF
    `s 102(b)(2) the certificate of incorporation contains the compromise or arrangement provision in haec verba` `my kind of corporation` `it uses the words of paragraph (b)(2)(i)` `it uses the words of paragraph (b)(2)(ii)`

@export May I apply to the court for a meeting of creditors or stockholders to be summoned under the compromise or arrangement provision (s 102(b)(2))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `who I am` IS AN Actor @desc Who are you? (The corporation; a creditor; a stockholder; a member of a nonstock corporation; a receiver; or a trustee.)
      `the certificate has the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain the compromise or arrangement provision?
      `I was appointed under section 291 or 279` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a receiver or a trustee: were you appointed for this corporation under section 291 or section 279 of Title 8?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to the court for a meeting to be summoned` IS
    `s 102(b)(2) the applicant may apply for a meeting to be summoned` `my kind of corporation` `who I am` `the certificate has the provision` `I was appointed under section 291 or 279`

@export Is the compromise or arrangement binding on me and on the others in my class (s 102(b)(2))?
GIVEN `members of the class who agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many creditors (or stockholders or members) in the class agreed to the compromise or arrangement?
      `members of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many creditors (or stockholders or members) are in the class, counted as the vote is counted?
      `value of those who agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc What value do those who agreed represent?
      `value of the class` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the class?
      `the court sanctioned it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court to which the application was made sanctioned the compromise or arrangement and the reorganization?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` IS
    `s 102(b)(2) the compromise or arrangement and the reorganization are binding on all` `members of the class who agreed` `members of the class` `value of those who agreed` `value of the class` `the court sanctioned it`

-- s 102(b)(3). Preemptive rights.
@export Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock (s 102(b)(3))?
GIVEN `the certificate expressly grants it to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation expressly grant you a preemptive right to subscribe to an additional issue of stock or to a security convertible into stock?
      `my right arose on` IS A DATE @desc If you rely on a right that was in existence on July 3, 1967, on what date did it arise? (Any date after July 3, 1967 if you do not rely on one.)
      `I rely on a right that existed in 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on a preemptive right that was in existence on July 3, 1967?
      `it was changed or terminated expressly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that right been changed or terminated by appropriate action that expressly provides for the change or termination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have a preemptive right to subscribe to the corporation's new stock` IF
    `s 102(b)(3) the stockholder has a preemptive right to subscribe to an additional issue of stock or to a convertible security` `the certificate expressly grants it to me` `the date my right arose` `it was changed or terminated expressly`
    WHERE
        `the date my right arose` MEANS IF `I rely on a right that existed in 1967` THEN JUST `my right arose on` ELSE NOTHING

@export May the certificate grant stockholders a preemptive right (s 102(b)(3))?
GIVEN `the provision grants a preemptive right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision grant the holders of the stock (or of a class or series) the preemptive right to subscribe to any or all additional issues of stock, or to securities convertible into it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate grant stockholders a preemptive right` IF
    `s 102(b)(3) the certificate of incorporation may contain the provision granting a preemptive right` `the provision grants a preemptive right`

-- s 102(b)(4). A larger vote, or a larger number of directors, than the chapter requires.
@export May the certificate require a larger vote of the stock than this Law requires for a corporate action (s 102(b)(4))?
GIVEN `the vote is counted against` IS A `Vote base` @desc Against what is the vote counted? (The same for the Law's requirement and the certificate's.)
      `the Law's fraction, top` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction of that base the Law requires, as top over bottom: what is the top? (For a majority, 1 over 2.)
      `the Law's fraction, bottom` IS A NUMBER @desc And the bottom? (For two thirds, 2 over 3.)
      `the Law's vote must be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the Law's fraction be exceeded (as for "a majority"), rather than merely reached (as for "at least")?
      `the certificate's fraction, top` IS A NUMBER @desc The fraction the certificate would require, as top over bottom: what is the top?
      `the certificate's fraction, bottom` IS A NUMBER @desc And the bottom?
      `the certificate's vote must be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the certificate's fraction be exceeded, rather than merely reached?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate require a larger vote than this Law requires` IS
    IF (`the Law's fraction, bottom` AT MOST 0) OR (`the certificate's fraction, bottom` AT MOST 0)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `s 102(b)(4) the certificate of incorporation requires a larger portion of the stock or other securities having voting power than this chapter requires` `the Law's vote` `the certificate's vote`
    WHERE
        `the Law's vote` MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS `the vote is counted against`
            proportion IS (`the Law's fraction, top` DIVIDED BY (IF `the Law's fraction, bottom` AT MOST 0 THEN 1 ELSE `the Law's fraction, bottom`))
            `must be exceeded` IS `the Law's vote must be exceeded`
        `the certificate's vote` MEANS `Vote requirement` WITH
            `counted against` IS `the vote is counted against`
            proportion IS (`the certificate's fraction, top` DIVIDED BY (IF `the certificate's fraction, bottom` AT MOST 0 THEN 1 ELSE `the certificate's fraction, bottom`))
            `must be exceeded` IS `the certificate's vote must be exceeded`

@export May the certificate require a larger number of the directors than this Law requires for a corporate action (s 102(b)(4))?
GIVEN `the number of directors the Law requires` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the Law require for the action?
      `the number of directors the certificate would require` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors would the certificate require?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate require a larger number of the directors than this Law requires` IF
    `s 102(b)(4) the certificate of incorporation requires a larger number of the directors than this chapter requires` `the number of directors the Law requires` `the number of directors the certificate would require`

-- s 102(b)(5)
@export Does the corporation have perpetual existence (s 102(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the certificate limits the duration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation limit the duration of the corporation's existence to a specified date?
      `the date it limits the duration to` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date? (Any date if it does not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation have perpetual existence` IF
    `s 102(b)(5) the corporation has perpetual existence` `the limit`
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS IF `the certificate limits the duration` THEN JUST `the date it limits the duration to` ELSE NOTHING

@export Has the duration of the corporation's existence expired on this day (s 102(b)(5))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc On what day are you asking?
      `the certificate limits the duration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation limit the duration of the corporation's existence to a specified date?
      `the date it limits the duration to` IS A DATE @desc If so, to what date? (Any date if it does not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the duration of the corporation's existence expired on this day` IF
    `s 102(b)(5) the duration of the corporation's existence has expired` `the day` `the limit`
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS IF `the certificate limits the duration` THEN JUST `the date it limits the duration to` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 102(b)(6). Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts?
@export Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts (s 102(b)(6))?
GIVEN `the certificate imposes liability on stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation contain a provision imposing personal liability for the corporation's debts on its stockholders?
      `its conditions are met as to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the conditions upon which it imposes liability met in your case?
      `I am liable for my own conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable for the debts by reason of your own conduct or acts (for example a guarantee you gave)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a stockholder, personally liable for the corporation's debts` IF
    `s 102(b)(6) the stockholder is personally liable for the payment of the corporation's debts` `the certificate imposes liability on stockholders` `its conditions are met as to me` `I am liable for my own conduct`

-- s 102(b)(7). A director or officer's liability for monetary damages: what the certificate may and may not shield.
@export May the certificate of incorporation eliminate or limit my personal liability for monetary damages for this breach of fiduciary duty (s 102(b)(7))?
GIVEN `I am sued as` IS A `s 102(b)(7) Capacity` @desc In what capacity is the liability asserted against you? (As a director; as a person who exercises the board's powers under the certificate; or as an officer.)
      `I am an officer deemed to have consented to service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an officer: were you, at the time of the act or omission, deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the corporation's registered agent under 10 Del. C. § 3114(b)?
      `it is a claim for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a claim by the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty as a director or officer?
      `it is a breach of loyalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a breach of your duty of loyalty to the corporation or its stockholders?
      `it is bad faith, intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for acts or omissions not in good faith, or involving intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law?
      `it is liability under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your liability as a director under section 174 of Title 8 (unlawful dividends or stock repurchases)?
      `I got an improper personal benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it for a transaction from which you derived an improper personal benefit?
      `it is by or in the right of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability asserted in an action by or in the right of the corporation?
      `the date of my act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the act or omission occur?
      `the date the provision became effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the certificate's provision eliminating or limiting liability become effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate eliminate or limit my personal liability for this breach` IS
    `s 102(b)(7) the provision may eliminate or limit the person's personal liability` `my liability`
    WHERE
        `my liability` MEANS `s 102(b)(7) Liability asserted` WITH
            capacity IS `I am sued as`
            `the officer was at the time of the act or omission deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to § 3114(b) of Title 10` IS `I am an officer deemed to have consented to service`
            `the liability is to the corporation or its stockholders for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty as a director or officer` IS `it is a claim for monetary damages for breach of fiduciary duty`
            `the liability is for a breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or its stockholders` IS `it is a breach of loyalty`
            `the liability is for acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law` IS `it is bad faith, intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law`
            `the liability is under § 174 of this title` IS `it is liability under section 174`
            `the person derived an improper personal benefit from the transaction` IS `I got an improper personal benefit`
            `the liability is asserted in an action by or in the right of the corporation` IS `it is by or in the right of the corporation`
            `the date of the act or omission` IS `the date of my act or omission`
            `the date when the provision becomes effective` IS `the date the provision became effective`

@export Does the exculpation provision, as it stood at the time of my act, still protect me after the corporation amended or repealed it (s 102(b)(7))?
GIVEN `the date of my act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the act or omission occur?
      `the date of the amendment or repeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the provision amended, repealed or eliminated?
      `the provision said otherwise when I acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the provision itself provide, at the time of the act or omission, that an amendment or repeal would affect it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the exculpation provision as it stood at the time of my act still protect me` IF
    `s 102(b)(7) the provision as it stood continues to apply to the act or omission despite the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `the date of my act or omission` `the date of the amendment or repeal` `the provision said otherwise when I acted`

-- s 102(c), (d), (f)
@export Must the certificate set out this power of the corporation (s 102(c))?
GIVEN `the power is conferred by this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power conferred on corporations by the Delaware General Corporation Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the certificate set out this power of the corporation` IS
    `s 102(c) the certificate of incorporation must set forth the power` `the power is conferred by this chapter`

@export May this provision of the certificate depend on facts that are ascertainable outside the certificate (s 102(d))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `s 102(d) Provision of the certificate` @desc Which provision is it?
      `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `the certificate says how the facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate clearly and explicitly set forth the manner in which the facts operate upon the provision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this provision depend on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` IF
    `s 102(d) the provision may be made dependent on facts ascertainable outside the certificate` `the provision` `my kind of corporation` `the certificate says how the facts operate`

@export Does this count as a fact on which a provision of the certificate may depend (s 102(d))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 102(d) Matter outside the certificate` @desc What is it? (An event; a determination by a person or body, including the corporation; an action by a person or body, including the corporation; or something else.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this count as a fact on which a provision may depend` IS
    `s 102(d) the matter is a fact on which a provision may depend` `the matter`

@export May the certificate make a stockholder liable for the fees or expenses of the corporation or another party in a claim (s 102(f))?
GIVEN `the provision would make a stockholder liable for fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the provision impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party?
      `the claim is a duty claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director, officer or stockholder in that capacity?
      `the Law gives Chancery jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Delaware General Corporation Law confer jurisdiction on the Court of Chancery over the claim?
      `a stockholder brought the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a claim that a stockholder, acting as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate make a stockholder liable for fees or expenses in a claim` IF
    `s 102(f) the certificate of incorporation may contain the provision` `the provision would make a stockholder liable for fees` `the claim is a duty claim` `the Law gives Chancery jurisdiction` `a stockholder brought the claim`

§§ `Reserving a name (section 102(e)) -- arises only if you want to reserve a corporate name`

@export May I reserve the exclusive right to use this name (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `s 102(e) Person reserving the name` @desc Which are you? (Someone intending to incorporate or organize a corporation with the name; a domestic corporation, or a foreign corporation qualified in Delaware, intending to change its name; a foreign corporation intending to qualify in Delaware and adopt the name; someone intending to organize a foreign corporation to qualify in Delaware and adopt the name; or another person.)
      `the name is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name available for use by a domestic or foreign corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I reserve the exclusive right to use this name` IF
    `s 102(e) the exclusive right to use the name may be reserved by or on behalf of the person` `who I am` `the name is available`

@export Is my application to reserve the name in the form required (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `I signed it as the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application executed by the applicant?
      `it certifies who the reservation is for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the reservation is made by or on behalf of a domestic corporation, foreign corporation or other person described in paragraphs (e)(1)-(4)?
      `it names the name to reserve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name to be reserved?
      `it gives my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name and address of the applicant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application to reserve the name in the form required` IF
    `s 102(e) the application to reserve a name is in the form required` `my application`
    WHERE
        `my application` MEANS `s 102(e) Application to reserve a name` WITH
            `the application is executed by the applicant` IS `I signed it as the applicant`
            `the application certifies that the reservation is made by or on behalf of a domestic corporation, foreign corporation or other person described in paragraphs (e)(1)-(4)` IS `it certifies who the reservation is for`
            `the application specifies the name to be reserved` IS `it names the name to reserve`
            `the application specifies the name and address of the applicant` IS `it gives my name and address`

@export Must the Secretary of State reserve the name for me for 120 days (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `my application is in the form required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application in the form the subsection requires?
      `the Secretary of State finds the name available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State found that the name is available for use by a domestic or foreign corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State reserve the name for me` IF
    `s 102(e) the Secretary of State must reserve the name for the applicant for a period of 120 days` `my application is in the form required` `the Secretary of State finds the name available`

@export Through what date does my name reservation last (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `the date it was reserved` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the name reserved?
      `times it was renewed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times has the reservation been renewed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Through what date does my name reservation last` IS
    `s 102(e) the last day of the reservation` `the date it was reserved` `times it was renewed`

@export Does my application for renewal renew the reservation (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `I signed the renewal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for renewal executed by the applicant?
      `it certifies who the renewal is for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify that the reservation is renewed by or on behalf of a domestic corporation, foreign corporation or other person described in paragraphs (e)(1)-(4)?
      `it names the reservation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name reservation to be renewed?
      `it gives my name and address for renewal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name and address of the applicant?
      `the date I filed it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file it with the Secretary of State?
      `the last day of the current reservation` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the reservation (or of the last renewal) now running?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application for renewal renew the reservation` IF
    `s 102(e) the application for renewal renews the reservation` `my renewal` `the last day of the current reservation`
    WHERE
        `my renewal` MEANS `s 102(e) Application for renewal` WITH
            `the application for renewal is executed by the applicant` IS `I signed the renewal`
            `the application for renewal certifies that the reservation is renewed by or on behalf of a domestic corporation, foreign corporation or other person described in paragraphs (e)(1)-(4)` IS `it certifies who the renewal is for`
            `the application for renewal specifies the name reservation to be renewed` IS `it names the reservation`
            `the application for renewal specifies the name and address of the applicant` IS `it gives my name and address for renewal`
            `the date on which the application for renewal was filed with the Secretary of State` IS `the date I filed it`

@export Has the right to the exclusive use of the reserved name been transferred (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `the notice is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice of the transfer been filed in the office of the Secretary of State?
      `the applicant signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it executed by the applicant for whom the name was reserved?
      `it names the reservation to transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name reservation to be transferred?
      `it gives the transferee's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name and address of the transferee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the right to the exclusive use of the reserved name been transferred` IF
    `s 102(e) the right to the exclusive use of the reserved name has been transferred` `my notice of transfer`
    WHERE
        `my notice of transfer` MEANS `s 102(e) Notice of transfer` WITH
            `the notice of transfer is filed in the office of the Secretary of State` IS `the notice is filed`
            `the notice of transfer is executed by the applicant for whom the name was reserved` IS `the applicant signed it`
            `the notice of transfer specifies the name reservation to be transferred` IS `it names the reservation to transfer`
            `the notice of transfer specifies the name and address of the transferee` IS `it gives the transferee's name and address`

@export Has the name reservation been cancelled (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `the notice of cancellation is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice of cancellation been filed with the Secretary of State?
      `the applicant or transferee signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it executed by the applicant or the transferee?
      `it names the reservation to cancel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name reservation to be cancelled?
      `it gives the signer's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the name and address of the applicant or transferee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the name reservation been cancelled` IF
    `s 102(e) the reservation has been cancelled` `my notice of cancellation`
    WHERE
        `my notice of cancellation` MEANS `s 102(e) Notice of cancellation` WITH
            `the notice of cancellation is filed with the Secretary of State` IS `the notice of cancellation is filed`
            `the notice of cancellation is executed by the applicant or transferee` IS `the applicant or transferee signed it`
            `the notice of cancellation specifies the name reservation to be cancelled` IS `it names the reservation to cancel`
            `the notice of cancellation specifies the name and address of the applicant or transferee` IS `it gives the signer's name and address`

@export Must the Secretary of State send me back a copy of my filed instrument, and what fee do I pay (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State finds it does not conform to law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State found that the application, renewal, notice of transfer or notice of cancellation does not conform to law?
      `all fees have been received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the filing fees required by law been received?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State send me back a copy of my filed instrument` IF
    `s 102(e) the Secretary of State must return a copy of the filed instrument with a notation of the action taken` `the Secretary of State finds it does not conform to law` `all fees have been received`

@export What fee must I pay with this filing about my name reservation (s 102(e))?
GIVEN `the filing` IS A `s 102(e) Filing concerning a reservation` @desc What are you filing? (The reservation of a name; its renewal; a notice of transfer; a notice of cancellation; or another filing.)
      `the amount section 391 sets` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does section 391 of Title 8 set for this filing, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What fee must I pay with this filing about my name reservation` IS
    `s 102(e) the fee payable at the time of the filing` `the filing` `the amount section 391 sets`

§§ `Signing, acknowledging and filing an instrument (section 103)`

-- s 103(a). Who signs: the incorporators sign the certificate (and an instrument filed before the initial board is
-- elected, if the certificate did not name the initial directors); the corporation's officers, directors or
-- stockholders sign all other instruments.
@export Do the incorporators sign this instrument, or the corporation's officers, directors or stockholders (s 103(a))?
GIVEN `it is the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument the certificate of incorporation?
      `it is to be filed before the initial board is elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors?
      `the certificate named the initial directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the initial directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the incorporators sign this instrument` IF
    `s 103(a)(1) the instrument is one that the incorporators sign` `my instrument`
    WHERE
        `my instrument` MEANS `s 103(a) Instrument` WITH
            `the instrument is the certificate of incorporation` IS `it is the certificate of incorporation`
            `the instrument is to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors` IS `it is to be filed before the initial board is elected`
            `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` IS `the certificate named the initial directors`

@export Has this certificate or early instrument been signed as the Law requires of the incorporators (s 103(a)(1))?
GIVEN `it is the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument the certificate of incorporation (rather than another instrument filed before the initial board is elected)?
      `every incorporator signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did every incorporator sign it?
      `the incorporators' successors or assigns signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incorporators' successors and assigns sign it (another instrument only)?
      `an incorporator is not available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an incorporator not available (another instrument only)?
      `the principal signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person for whom or on whose behalf the unavailable incorporator acted, directly or indirectly, as employee or agent sign it?
      `it says the incorporator is unavailable and why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument state that the incorporator is not available and the reason?
      `it says the incorporator acted for that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the incorporator, in executing the certificate, acted as employee or agent for or on behalf of that person?
      `it says that person's signature is authorized and not wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that that person's signature on the instrument is otherwise authorized and not wrongful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has this certificate or early instrument been signed as the Law requires of the incorporators` IF
    `s 103(a)(1) the instrument is signed as required of the incorporators` `my instrument` `my incorporator signing`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders (TRUE or FALSE): the rule called below does not read those fields of the record.
        `my instrument` MEANS `s 103(a) Instrument` WITH
            `the instrument is the certificate of incorporation` IS `it is the certificate of incorporation`
            `the instrument is to be filed before the election of the initial board of directors` IS TRUE
            `the initial directors were named in the certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE
        `my incorporator signing` MEANS `s 103(a)(1) Signing by the incorporators` WITH
            `every incorporator signed` IS `every incorporator signed`
            `the successors and assigns of the incorporators signed` IS `the incorporators' successors or assigns signed`
            `an incorporator is not available` IS `an incorporator is not available`
            `a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator acted as employee or agent signed` IS `the principal signed`
            `the instrument states that the incorporator is not available and the reason` IS `it says the incorporator is unavailable and why`
            `the instrument states that the incorporator in executing the certificate acted as employee or agent for or on behalf of that person` IS `it says the incorporator acted for that person`
            `the instrument states that that person's signature is otherwise authorized and not wrongful` IS `it says that person's signature is authorized and not wrongful`

@export Has this instrument been signed as the Law requires for the corporation (s 103(a)(2))?
GIVEN `an authorized officer signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an authorized officer of the corporation sign it?
      `it shows there are no officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear from the instrument that the corporation has no officers?
      `a majority of the directors signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a majority of the directors sign it?
      `directors the board designated signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did such directors as the board designated sign it?
      `it shows there are no officers or directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear from the instrument that the corporation has no officers or directors?
      `holders of a majority of the shares signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the holders of record of a majority of all outstanding shares sign it?
      `holders they designated signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did such of the holders of record as the holders of a majority of the outstanding shares designated sign it?
      `holders of all the shares signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the holders of record of all the outstanding shares sign it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has this instrument been signed as the Law requires for the corporation` IF
    `s 103(a)(2) the instrument is signed as required for the corporation` `my corporation signing`
    WHERE
        `my corporation signing` MEANS `s 103(a)(2) Signing for the corporation` WITH
            `an authorized officer of the corporation signed` IS `an authorized officer signed`
            `it appears from the instrument that there are no such officers` IS `it shows there are no officers`
            `a majority of the directors signed` IS `a majority of the directors signed`
            `such directors as the board designated signed` IS `directors the board designated signed`
            `it appears from the instrument that there are no such officers or directors` IS `it shows there are no officers or directors`
            `the holders of record of a majority of all outstanding shares of stock signed` IS `holders of a majority of the shares signed`
            `such of the holders of record as the holders of a majority of all outstanding shares designated signed` IS `holders they designated signed`
            `the holders of record of all outstanding shares of stock signed` IS `holders of all the shares signed`

-- s 103(b). Acknowledgment.
@export Is the acknowledgment requirement satisfied for this instrument (s 103(b))?
GIVEN `it was signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument signed?
      `a signer acknowledged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person signing acknowledge that it is that person's act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation, and that the facts stated in it are true?
      `before a person authorized to take acknowledgments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acknowledgment made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds?
      `that person has a seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person have a seal of office?
      `that person affixed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person affix the seal to the instrument?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the acknowledgment requirement satisfied for this instrument` IF
    `s 103(b) the requirement that the instrument be acknowledged is satisfied` `my acknowledgment`
    WHERE
        `my acknowledgment` MEANS `s 103(b) Acknowledgment` WITH
            `the instrument was signed` IS `it was signed`
            `a person signing acknowledged that the instrument is that person's act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation and that the facts stated in it are true` IS `a signer acknowledged it`
            `the acknowledgment was made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds` IS `before a person authorized to take acknowledgments`
            `that person has a seal of office` IS `that person has a seal`
            `that person affixed the seal of office to the instrument` IS `that person affixed it`

@export By signing alone, do I affirm under penalties of perjury that the facts stated are true (s 103(b)(2))?
GIVEN `I signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sign the instrument?
      `a signer acknowledged it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person signing also formally acknowledge that it is that person's act and deed, or the corporation's, and that the facts stated are true?
      `before a person authorized to take acknowledgments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that acknowledgment made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds?
      `that person has a seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person have a seal of office?
      `that person affixed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person affix the seal to the instrument?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `By signing alone, do I affirm under penalties of perjury that the facts stated are true` IF
    `s 103(b)(2) the signatory affirms under penalties of perjury that the facts stated are true` `my acknowledgment`
    WHERE
        `my acknowledgment` MEANS `s 103(b) Acknowledgment` WITH
            `the instrument was signed` IS `I signed`
            `a person signing acknowledged that the instrument is that person's act and deed or the act and deed of the corporation and that the facts stated in it are true` IS `a signer acknowledged it`
            `the acknowledgment was made before a person authorized by the law of the place of execution to take acknowledgments of deeds` IS `before a person authorized to take acknowledgments`
            `that person has a seal of office` IS `that person has a seal`
            `that person affixed the seal of office to the instrument` IS `that person affixed it`

@export As of what date must the facts I affirm by signing be true (s 103(b)(2))?
GIVEN `the date the instrument was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the instrument filed?
      `the instrument names a later effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument provide that it is not to become effective until a later date?
      `that later date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `As of what date must the facts I affirm by signing be true` IS
    CONSIDER `s 103(d) the date on which the instrument is effective` `the date the instrument was filed` `the later date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST effective THEN JUST (`s 103(b)(2) the date as of which the facts stated by a signatory relying on the signature alone must be true` effective)
    WHERE
        `the later date` MEANS IF `the instrument names a later effective date` THEN JUST `that later date` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 103(c). Filing.
@export Have I done everything that filing requires of me (s 103(c)(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the signed instrument to the office of the Secretary of State?
      `I tendered all the taxes and fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tender all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done everything that filing requires of me` IF
    `s 103(c)(1) and (2) the filer has done what filing requires of the filer` `my filing steps`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders (TRUE or FALSE): the rule called below does not read those fields of the record.
        `my filing steps` MEANS `s 103(c) Steps of filing` WITH
            `the signed instrument was delivered to the office of the Secretary of State` IS `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office`
            `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered` IS `I tendered all the taxes and fees`
            `the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument due to an error, omission or other imperfection` IS FALSE
            `the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word Filed and the date and time of its filing` IS FALSE

@export Must the Secretary of State certify my instrument as filed (s 103(c)(3))?
GIVEN `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the signed instrument to the office of the Secretary of State?
      `I tendered all the taxes and fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tender all the taxes and fees?
      `the Secretary of State refused it for an error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State refused to file it because of an error, omission or other imperfection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary of State certify my instrument as filed` IF
    `s 103(c)(3) the Secretary of State must certify the instrument as filed` `my filing steps`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders (TRUE or FALSE): the rule called below does not read those fields of the record.
        `my filing steps` MEANS `s 103(c) Steps of filing` WITH
            `the signed instrument was delivered to the office of the Secretary of State` IS `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office`
            `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered` IS `I tendered all the taxes and fees`
            `the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument due to an error, omission or other imperfection` IS `the Secretary of State refused it for an error`
            `the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word Filed and the date and time of its filing` IS FALSE

@export Is my instrument filed (s 103(c))?
GIVEN `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the signed instrument to the office of the Secretary of State?
      `I tendered all the taxes and fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tender all the taxes and fees?
      `it is endorsed Filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word "Filed" and the date and time of its filing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(c), is my instrument filed` IF
    `s 103(c) the instrument has been filed` `my filing steps`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders (TRUE or FALSE): the rule called below does not read those fields of the record.
        `my filing steps` MEANS `s 103(c) Steps of filing` WITH
            `the signed instrument was delivered to the office of the Secretary of State` IS `I delivered the signed instrument to the Secretary of State's office`
            `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered` IS `I tendered all the taxes and fees`
            `the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument due to an error, omission or other imperfection` IS FALSE
            `the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word Filed and the date and time of its filing` IS `it is endorsed Filed`

@export May the Secretary of State hold my instrument in suspension, and what does that cost my corporation (s 103(c)(4))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State refused it for an error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument because of an error, omission or other imperfection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State hold my instrument in suspension` IF
    `s 103(c)(4) the Secretary of State may hold the instrument in suspension` `my filing steps`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders (TRUE or FALSE): the rule called below does not read those fields of the record.
        `my filing steps` MEANS `s 103(c) Steps of filing` WITH
            `the signed instrument was delivered to the office of the Secretary of State` IS FALSE
            `all taxes and fees authorized by law to be collected by the Secretary of State in connection with the filing were tendered` IS FALSE
            `the Secretary of State refused to file the instrument due to an error, omission or other imperfection` IS `the Secretary of State refused it for an error`
            `the Secretary of State endorsed the signed instrument with the word Filed and the date and time of its filing` IS FALSE

@export Is the Secretary of State barred from issuing my corporation a certificate of good standing (s 103(c)(4))?
GIVEN `an instrument of my corporation is held in suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an instrument of the corporation being held in suspension under paragraph (c)(4)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State barred from issuing my corporation a certificate of good standing` IF
    `s 103(c)(4) the Secretary of State is barred from issuing a certificate of good standing` `an instrument of my corporation is held in suspension`

DECLARE `How the filing date of my instrument is set` IS ONE OF
    `the date I delivered it`
    `a later date that I asked for and the Secretary of State set`
    `the replacement of an instrument held in suspension`
    `the date the Secretary of State entered the information`
    `an earlier date set because of an extraordinary condition`

@export What is my instrument's filing date (s 103(c)(3), (4))?
GIVEN `how it is set` IS A `How the filing date of my instrument is set` @desc How is the filing date set? (By the date you delivered it; at a later date you asked for; by the replacement of an instrument held in suspension; by the date the information was entered; or at an earlier date set because of an extraordinary condition.)
      `the date I delivered it on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deliver the instrument?
      `the later date set` IS A DATE @desc If a later date was set at your request: what date? (Any date otherwise.)
      `the date the rejected instrument would have been filed` IS A DATE @desc If this is a replacement: what filing date would the rejected instrument have had if accepted?
      `business days to replace it` IS A NUMBER @desc If this is a replacement: how many business days after notice of the suspension was the replacement delivered?
      `the replacement was proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If this is a replacement: was it in proper form for filing, with the required taxes and fees tendered?
      `the date the information was entered` IS A DATE @desc If the Secretary of State entered the information from the instrument before you delivered it: on what date?
      `hours from entry to delivery` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after the information was entered did you deliver the instrument?
      `delivered on that same date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver the instrument on the date the information was entered?
      `the earlier date set` IS A DATE @desc If an earlier date was set because of an extraordinary condition: what date?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 103(c), what is my instrument's filing date` IS
    `s 103(c)(3) the filing date of the instrument` `my route` `the date I delivered it on`
    WHERE
        `my route` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it is set`
            WHEN `the date I delivered it` THEN `the date of delivery`
            WHEN `a later date that I asked for and the Secretary of State set` THEN `a later date established on request made on or before delivery` `the later date set`
            WHEN `the replacement of an instrument held in suspension` THEN `replacement of an instrument held in suspension` `the date the rejected instrument would have been filed` `business days to replace it` `the replacement was proper`
            WHEN `the date the Secretary of State entered the information` THEN `entry of the information under paragraph (c)(8)` `the date the information was entered` `hours from entry to delivery` `delivered on that same date`
            WHEN `an earlier date set because of an extraordinary condition` THEN `an earlier date established under subsection (i)` `the earlier date set`

@export What county assessment fee must I tender with my instrument, in dollars (s 103(c)(6))?
GIVEN `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the instrument?
      `it is a certificate of dissolution of the kind section 391(a)(5)b. names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under section 391(a)(5)b. of Title 8?
      `it is a document under subchapter XVI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI of the Delaware General Corporation Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What county assessment fee must I tender with my instrument` IS
    `s 103(c)(6) the county assessment fee` `the number of pages` `it is a certificate of dissolution of the kind section 391(a)(5)b. names` `it is a document under subchapter XVI`

@export What courthouse municipality fee must I tender with my instrument, in dollars (s 103(c)(7))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate of dissolution of the kind section 391(a)(5)b. names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a certificate of dissolution qualifying for treatment under section 391(a)(5)b. of Title 8?
      `it is a resignation of agent without a successor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a resignation of agent without appointment of a successor under section 136?
      `it is a document under subchapter XVI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a document filed in accordance with subchapter XVI of the Delaware General Corporation Law?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What courthouse municipality fee must I tender with my instrument` IS
    `s 103(c)(7) the courthouse municipality fee` `it is a certificate of dissolution of the kind section 391(a)(5)b. names` `it is a resignation of agent without a successor` `it is a document under subchapter XVI`

-- s 103(d). Effective date.
@export May my instrument say that it becomes effective on a later date (s 103(d))?
GIVEN `the date of filing` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the instrument filed?
      `the later date I want` IS A DATE @desc On what later date do you want it to become effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my instrument say that it becomes effective on a later date` IS
    `s 103(d) the instrument may become effective on the specified later date` `the date of filing` `the later date I want`

@export On what date is my instrument effective (s 103(d))?
GIVEN `the date of filing` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the instrument filed?
      `it names a later effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument provide that it is not to become effective until a specified later date?
      `that later date` IS A DATE @desc If so, what date? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under section 103(d), on what date is my instrument effective` IS
    `s 103(d) the date on which the instrument is effective` `the date of filing` `the later date`
    WHERE
        `the later date` MEANS IF `it names a later effective date` THEN JUST `that later date` ELSE NOTHING

@export Have I validly terminated or amended an instrument that has a future effective date (s 103(d))?
GIVEN `the date I filed the certificate` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the certificate of termination or amendment?
      `it was executed under subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it executed in accordance with subsection (a)?
      `it identifies the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it identify the instrument that has been terminated or amended?
      `it says how` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the instrument has been terminated, or the manner in which it has been amended?
      `the future effective date` IS A DATE @desc What is the future effective date set forth in the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I validly terminated or amended an instrument that has a future effective date` IS
    `s 103(d) the future effective instrument has been terminated or amended by a certificate in due form and time` `my certificate` `the future effective date`
    WHERE
        `my certificate` MEANS `s 103(d) Certificate of termination or amendment` WITH
            `the date on which the certificate was filed` IS `the date I filed the certificate`
            `the certificate was executed in accordance with subsection (a)` IS `it was executed under subsection (a)`
            `the certificate identifies the instrument which has been terminated or amended` IS `it identifies the instrument`
            `the certificate states that the instrument has been terminated or the manner in which it has been amended` IS `it says how`

-- s 103(e)
@export Does another section of the Law govern how this instrument is executed, acknowledged or filed, or when it becomes effective (s 103(e))?
GIVEN `another section prescribes a manner or time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another section of the Delaware General Corporation Law specifically prescribe a manner of executing, acknowledging or filing this instrument, or a time when it becomes effective?
      `it differs from section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that manner or time differ from the corresponding provisions of section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(e), does another section of the Law govern this instrument` IF
    `s 103(e) the other section governs` `another section prescribes a manner or time` `it differs from section 103`

-- s 103(f). Correction.
@export May a filed instrument be corrected or nullified by a certificate of correction (s 103(f))?
GIVEN `it was filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the instrument authorized to be filed with the Secretary of State under a provision of Title 8, and has it been filed?
      `it is an inaccurate record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an inaccurate record of the corporate action it refers to?
      `it was defectively executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it defectively or erroneously executed, sealed or acknowledged?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a filed instrument be corrected or nullified by a certificate of correction` IF
    `s 103(f) the instrument may be corrected or nullified by a certificate of correction` `my filed instrument`
    WHERE
        `my filed instrument` MEANS `s 103(f) Filed instrument` WITH
            `the instrument was authorized to be filed with the Secretary of State under a provision of this title and has been filed` IS `it was filed`
            `the instrument is an inaccurate record of the corporate action it refers to` IS `it is an inaccurate record`
            `the instrument was defectively or erroneously executed, sealed or acknowledged` IS `it was defectively executed`

@export Is my certificate of correction in the form the Law requires (s 103(f))?
GIVEN `it was executed, acknowledged and filed under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103?
      `it corrects and does not nullify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it correct the instrument (rather than nullify it)?
      `it specifies the inaccuracy or defect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the inaccuracy or defect?
      `it sets out the corrected portion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it corrects: does it set forth the portion of the instrument in corrected form?
      `it provides for nullification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it nullifies: does it provide for the nullification of the instrument?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my certificate of correction in the form the Law requires` IF
    `s 103(f) the certificate of correction is in the form required` `my certificate of correction`
    WHERE
        `my certificate of correction` MEANS `s 103(f) Certificate of correction` WITH
            `the certificate was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with this section` IS `it was executed, acknowledged and filed under section 103`
            `the instrument is to be corrected (and not nullified)` IS `it corrects and does not nullify`
            `the certificate specifies the inaccuracy or defect` IS `it specifies the inaccuracy or defect`
            `the certificate sets forth the portion of the instrument in corrected form` IS `it sets out the corrected portion`
            `the certificate provides for the nullification of the instrument` IS `it provides for nullification`

@export Is my corrected instrument in the form the Law requires (s 103(f))?
GIVEN `it was executed, acknowledged and filed under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the corrected instrument executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103?
      `it is designated as corrected in its heading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it specifically designated as a corrected instrument in its heading?
      `it specifies the inaccuracy or defect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the inaccuracy or defect to be corrected?
      `it sets out the whole instrument corrected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the entire instrument in corrected form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corrected instrument in the form the Law requires` IF
    `s 103(f) the corrected instrument is in the form required` `my corrected instrument`
    WHERE
        `my corrected instrument` MEANS `s 103(f) Corrected instrument` WITH
            `the corrected instrument was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with this section` IS `it was executed, acknowledged and filed under section 103`
            `the corrected instrument is specifically designated as such in its heading` IS `it is designated as corrected in its heading`
            `the corrected instrument specifies the inaccuracy or defect to be corrected` IS `it specifies the inaccuracy or defect`
            `the corrected instrument sets forth the entire instrument in corrected form` IS `it sets out the whole instrument corrected`

@export From what date is a corrected or nullified instrument effective as against me (s 103(f))?
GIVEN `the date the original was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the original instrument filed?
      `the date the correction was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate of correction (or corrected instrument) filed?
      `I am substantially and adversely affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you substantially and adversely affected by the correction or nullification?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what date is a corrected or nullified instrument effective as against me` IS
    `s 103(f) the date from which the corrected or nullified instrument is effective as to the person` `the date the original was filed` `the date the correction was filed` `I am substantially and adversely affected`

-- s 103(g), (h)
@export Can I hold the Secretary of State liable for this act in relation to my instrument (s 103(g))?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `s 103(g) Act of the Secretary of State` @desc What did the Secretary of State do? (Preclearance for filing; acceptance for filing; filing and indexing; or another act.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I hold the Secretary of State liable for this act` IS
    `s 103(g) the Secretary of State is liable to any person for the act` `the act`

@export May I sign this instrument in this form (s 103(h))?
GIVEN `the form of signature` IS A `s 103(h) Form of signature` @desc What form is the signature? (Manual; facsimile; conformed; electronically transmitted; or another form.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 103(h), may I sign this instrument in this form` IS
    `s 103(h) the form of signature is permitted on an instrument authorized to be filed` `the form of signature`

-- s 103(j)
@export Must my corporation amend an old certificate or document to state its registered office as section 131(c) requires (s 103(j))?
GIVEN `the date it was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate or other document filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation amend an old document to comply with section 131(c)` IS
    IF `s 103(j) the corporation need not amend the document to comply with § 131(c)` `the date it was filed`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@export Must a new certificate or document that changes the address of the registered office comply with section 131(c) (s 103(j))?
GIVEN `the date it was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate or other document filed?
      `it changes the registered office address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it change the address of a registered office?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a new document that changes the registered office address comply with section 131(c)` IS
    `s 103(j) the document must comply with § 131(c)` `the date it was filed` `it changes the registered office address`

§§ `If a filing was attempted but failed because of an extraordinary condition (section 103(i)) -- arises only after such a failed attempt`

@export May the Secretary of State give my instrument the earlier filing date because of an extraordinary condition (s 103(i)(1))?
GIVEN `I delivered an affidavit of extraordinary condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver, with the actual delivery of the instrument and tender of the taxes and fees, a separate affidavit headed "affidavit of extraordinary condition"?
      `it attests a good faith earlier effort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit attest that an earlier effort to deliver the instrument and tender the taxes and fees was made in good faith?
      `it gives the details and asks for that date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it specify the nature, date and time of that effort and ask the Secretary of State to establish that date and time as the filing date?
      `the Secretary of State waived the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Instead: did the Secretary of State give a written waiver of the affidavit upon the actual delivery and tender?
      `the Secretary of State finds an extraordinary condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State determined that an extraordinary condition existed at that date and time?
      `it finds the earlier effort failed because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it determined that the earlier effort was unsuccessful as a result of that condition?
      `it finds the delivery within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it determined that the actual delivery and tender were made within a reasonable period after the condition ended?
      `business days after the condition ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after the condition ended were the actual delivery and tender made?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State give my instrument the earlier filing date` IF
    `s 103(i)(1) the Secretary of State may establish the earlier date and time as the filing date` `my request`
    WHERE
        `my request` MEANS `s 103(i)(1) Request for an earlier filing date` WITH
            `an affidavit headed affidavit of extraordinary condition was delivered with the actual delivery of the instrument and tender of the required taxes and fees` IS `I delivered an affidavit of extraordinary condition`
            `the affidavit attests that an earlier effort to deliver the instrument and tender the taxes and fees was made in good faith` IS `it attests a good faith earlier effort`
            `the affidavit specifies the nature, date and time of that effort and requests that the Secretary of State establish that date and time` IS `it gives the details and asks for that date`
            `the Secretary of State provided a written waiver of the affidavit upon the actual delivery and tender` IS `the Secretary of State waived the affidavit`
            `the Secretary of State determines that an extraordinary condition existed at that date and time` IS `the Secretary of State finds an extraordinary condition`
            `the Secretary of State determines that the earlier effort was unsuccessful as a result of that condition` IS `it finds the earlier effort failed because of it`
            `the Secretary of State determines that the actual delivery and tender were made within a reasonable period after the cessation of the condition` IS `it finds the delivery within a reasonable period`
            `the number of business days from the cessation of the condition to the actual delivery and tender` IS `business days after the condition ended`

@export Must I pay a fee for the Secretary of State's receiving my affidavit of extraordinary condition, and how much (s 103(i)(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fee must I pay for the Secretary of State's receiving my affidavit of extraordinary condition` IS
    `s 103(i)(1) the fee payable to the Secretary of State for receiving an affidavit of extraordinary condition`

@export Was it an extraordinary condition (s 103(i)(2))?
GIVEN `the event` IS A `s 103(i)(2) Event` @desc What happened? (An attack, invasion or occupation by foreign military forces; a disaster, war, armed conflict, revolution, insurrection or civil commotion; a malfunction or outage of electricity or telephone service to the Secretary of State's office; weather or another condition in the locality; or another event.)
      `the place` IS A `s 103(i)(2) Place` @desc Where? (The United States; a locality in which the Secretary of State conducts its business; the locality in which you made the good faith effort; or somewhere else.)
      `it was an emergency or the immediate threat of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there an emergency resulting from the event, or the immediate threat of it?
      `the office was closed or filing took extraordinary effort` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result, was the Secretary of State's office not open for filing, or could filing not be effected without extraordinary effort?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it an extraordinary condition` IF
    `s 103(i)(2) there is an extraordinary condition` `the event` `the place` `it was an emergency or the immediate threat of one` `the office was closed or filing took extraordinary effort`

@export Is the Secretary of State's determination about the extraordinary condition conclusive against me (s 103(i)(2))?
GIVEN `there was actual fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there actual fraud?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Secretary of State's determination about the extraordinary condition conclusive against me` IF
    `s 103(i)(2) the determination of the Secretary of State is conclusive` `there was actual fraud`

@export From what date is my instrument effective as against me, after the Secretary of State set an earlier filing date (s 103(i)(3))?
GIVEN `the earlier date the Secretary of State set` IS A DATE @desc What filing date did the Secretary of State establish under subsection (i)?
      `the date endorsed on the affidavit or waiver` IS A DATE @desc What date is endorsed on the affidavit of extraordinary condition or the written waiver?
      `I am substantially and adversely affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you substantially and adversely affected by that establishment?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under section 103(i)(3), from what date is my instrument effective as against me` IS
    `s 103(i)(3) the date from which the instrument is effective as to the person` `the earlier date the Secretary of State set` `the date endorsed on the affidavit or waiver` `I am substantially and adversely affected`

§§ `The organization meeting (section 108)`

-- s 108(a). After the certificate is filed, an organization meeting is held of the incorporators or, if the initial
-- directors were named in the certificate, of the board, at the call of a majority of them.
@export Is the organization meeting a meeting of the board and not of the incorporators (s 108(a))?
GIVEN `the certificate named the initial directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the initial directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the organization meeting a meeting of the board and not of the incorporators` IF
    `s 108(a) the organization meeting is a meeting of the board of directors and not of the incorporators` `the certificate named the initial directors`

@export Is the organization meeting validly called by a majority of the incorporators or directors (s 108(a))?
GIVEN `the certificate named the initial directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the initial directors?
      `those who called it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many incorporators (or, if the initial directors were named, directors) called the meeting?
      `all of them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many incorporators (or directors) are there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the organization meeting validly called by a majority` IS
    `s 108(a) the call of the organization meeting is made by a majority of the incorporators or directors` `the certificate named the initial directors` `those who called it` `all of them`

@export May the organization meeting be held at this place (s 108(a))?
GIVEN `the place` IS A `s 108(a) Place of the organization meeting` @desc Is it within this State or without this State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the organization meeting be held at this place` IF
    `s 108(a) the organization meeting may be held at the place` `the place`

@export May this be done at the organization meeting (s 108(a))?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 108(a) Purpose of the organization meeting` @desc What do you want to do at the meeting?
      `the meeting is of the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a meeting of the board of directors (and not of the incorporators)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this be done at the organization meeting` IF
    `s 108(a) the purpose may be pursued at the organization meeting` `the purpose` `the meeting is of the board`

-- s 108(b). What notice is owed to me, and what notice I owe.
@export Is the notice I was given of the organization meeting enough (s 108(b))?
GIVEN `the day I was given notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was notice of the meeting given to you?
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
      `the notice was in writing or electronic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice in writing, or by electronic transmission, by a usual means of communication?
      `the notice stated time, place and purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it state the time, place and purposes of the meeting as fixed by the persons calling it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice I was given of the organization meeting enough` IF
    `s 108(b) the notice of the organization meeting is sufficient` `the day I was given notice` `the day of the meeting` `the notice was in writing or electronic` `the notice stated time, place and purposes`

@export Must I, as a person calling the organization meeting, give notice of it to this incorporator or director (s 108(b))?
GIVEN `they attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will or did the incorporator or director attend the meeting?
      `they waived notice before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incorporator or director waive notice before the meeting?
      `they waived notice after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the incorporator or director waive notice after the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give notice of the organization meeting to this incorporator or director` IF
    NOT (`s 108(b) notice of the meeting need not be given to the person` `they attend the meeting` `they waived notice before` `they waived notice after`)

-- s 108(c)
@export May the incorporators or directors act without holding the organization meeting (s 108(c))?
GIVEN `the certificate restricts it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation restrict action without a meeting?
      `how many of us there are` IS A NUMBER @desc How many incorporators (or, if the initial directors were named, directors) are there?
      `how many consent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them consent in writing or by electronic transmission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the incorporators or directors act without holding the organization meeting` IS
    `s 108(c) the action may be taken without a meeting` `the certificate restricts it` `how many of us there are` `how many consent`

@export Is my consent, which I arranged to take effect at a future time, deemed given at that time (s 108(c))?
GIVEN `the day I gave the instruction` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give the instruction, or make the provision, that the consent be effective at a future time?
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the consent to take effect?
      `I am then an incorporator or director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you then be an incorporator or director, as the case may be?
      `I revoked it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you revoke the consent before it took effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my consent given for a future time deemed given at that time` IS
    `s 108(c) the consent given for a future time is deemed given at that time` `the day I gave the instruction` `the day it takes effect` `I am then an incorporator or director` `I revoked it before`

@export Can I still revoke my consent that takes effect at a future time (s 108(c))?
GIVEN `the day I revoke it` IS A DATE @desc On what date would you revoke the consent?
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the consent to take effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still revoke my consent that takes effect at a future time` IS
    `s 108(c) the consent may still be revoked` `the day I revoke it` `the day it takes effect`

-- s 108(d)
@export As the person for whom an unavailable incorporator acted, may I take the incorporator's action (s 108(d))?
GIVEN `an incorporator is not available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an incorporator not available to act?
      `I am the person the incorporator acted for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person for whom or on whose behalf the incorporator was acting, directly or indirectly, as employee or agent?
      `my instrument or record says the incorporator is unavailable and why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument you sign, or the record of the meeting in which you participate, state that the incorporator is not available and the reason?
      `it says the incorporator acted for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the incorporator was acting directly or indirectly as employee or agent for or on behalf of you?
      `it says my signature or participation is authorized and not wrongful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that your signature or participation is otherwise authorized and not wrongful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As the person for whom an unavailable incorporator acted, may I take the incorporator's action` IF
    `s 108(d) the person may take the action that the incorporator would have been authorized to take under this section or § 107` `an incorporator is not available` `I am the person the incorporator acted for` `my instrument or record says the incorporator is unavailable and why` `it says the incorporator acted for me` `it says my signature or participation is authorized and not wrongful`

§§ `Bylaws (section 109)`

-- s 109(a). Who holds the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws.
@export Do I have the power to adopt, amend or repeal the bylaws (s 109(a))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `s 109(a) Holder of the power over the bylaws` @desc Which are you? (An incorporator; an initial director named in the certificate; an initial member of the governing body named in the certificate; a director before the corporation has received any payment for its stock; a stockholder entitled to vote, after payment; a member entitled to vote in a nonstock corporation; or a director or governing body member on whom the certificate confers the power.)
      `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `the initial directors or members were named` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation name the initial directors (or, for a nonstock corporation, the initial members of the governing body)?
      `the corporation has been paid for stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation received any payment for any of its stock?
      `the certificate gives the directors the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation confer the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors (or the governing body)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have the power to adopt, amend or repeal the bylaws` IF
    `s 109(a) the holder has the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws` `who I am` `my kind of corporation` `the initial directors or members were named` `the corporation has been paid for stock` `the certificate gives the directors the power`

@export Does giving the directors the power to amend the bylaws take that power away from the stockholders (s 109(a))?
GIVEN `the certificate gives the directors the power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate of incorporation confer the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors (or the governing body)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does giving the directors the power to amend the bylaws take that power away from the stockholders` IF
    `s 109(a) the conferral of the power on the directors or governing body divests the stockholders or members of the power` `the certificate gives the directors the power`

-- s 109(b)
@export May the bylaws contain this provision (s 109(b))?
GIVEN `it concerns the business, affairs, rights or powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision relate to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or its rights or powers or the rights or powers of its stockholders, directors, officers or employees?
      `it conflicts with law or the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision inconsistent with law or with the certificate of incorporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 109(b), may the bylaws contain this provision` IF
    `s 109(b) the bylaws may contain the provision` `it concerns the business, affairs, rights or powers` `it conflicts with law or the certificate`

@export May the bylaws make me, as a stockholder, liable for the fees or expenses of the corporation or another party in a claim (s 109(b))?
GIVEN `the bylaw would make a stockholder liable for fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the bylaw impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party?
      `the claim is a duty claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director, officer or stockholder in that capacity?
      `the Law gives Chancery jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Delaware General Corporation Law confer jurisdiction on the Court of Chancery over the claim?
      `a stockholder brought the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a claim that a stockholder, acting as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the bylaws make me liable for fees or expenses in a claim` IF
    `s 109(b) the bylaws may contain the provision on fees and expenses` `the bylaw would make a stockholder liable for fees` `the claim is a duty claim` `the Law gives Chancery jurisdiction` `a stockholder brought the claim`

§§ `Emergency bylaws and emergency powers (section 110) -- arises only during an emergency, or when preparing for one`

-- s 110(a)
@export Are the emergency bylaws operative now (s 110(a), (e))?
GIVEN `the emergency` IS A `s 110(a) Emergency` @desc What is the emergency? (An attack on the United States or on a locality where the corporation does business or holds meetings; a nuclear or atomic disaster; a catastrophe, including an epidemic or pandemic or a declaration of a national emergency; another similar emergency condition; or none.)
      `emergency bylaws have been adopted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have emergency bylaws been adopted?
      `the emergency is over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the emergency terminated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the emergency bylaws operative now` IF
    `s 110(a) the emergency bylaws are operative` `the emergency` `emergency bylaws have been adopted` `the emergency is over`

@export Were the emergency bylaws validly adopted (s 110(a))?
GIVEN `a quorum can readily be convened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a quorum of the board of directors be readily convened for a meeting?
      `the board adopted them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors adopt the emergency bylaws?
      `directors present who voted for them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the directors present voted to adopt them?
      `directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were present?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the emergency bylaws validly adopted` IS
    `s 110(a) the emergency bylaws were validly adopted` `a quorum can readily be convened` `the board adopted them` `directors present who voted for them` `directors present`

@export As a stockholder, can I repeal or change the emergency bylaws the board adopted (s 110(a))?
GIVEN `the board adopted them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the emergency bylaws adopted by the board of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a stockholder, can I repeal or change the emergency bylaws the board adopted` IF
    `s 110(a) the emergency bylaws are subject to repeal or change by action of the stockholders` `the board adopted them`

@export May the emergency bylaws make this provision (s 110(a))?
GIVEN `it is practical and necessary for the emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision practical and necessary for the circumstances of the emergency?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the emergency bylaws make this provision` IF
    `s 110(a) the emergency bylaws may make the provision` `it is practical and necessary for the emergency`

@export As an officer or director, may I call a meeting of the board during the emergency (s 110(a)(1))?
GIVEN `I am an officer or a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or a director?
      `I call it as the emergency bylaws prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you calling it in the manner and on the conditions the emergency bylaws prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As an officer or director, may I call a meeting of the board during the emergency` IF
    `s 110(a)(1) the person may call a meeting of the board of directors or a committee` `I am an officer or a director` `I call it as the emergency bylaws prescribe`

@export Do the directors who are present form a quorum at an emergency meeting (s 110(a)(2))?
GIVEN `directors in attendance` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are in attendance?
      `the emergency bylaws fix a greater number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the emergency bylaws fix a greater number as a quorum?
      `that greater number` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what number? (Any number if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the directors who are present form a quorum at an emergency meeting` IF
    `s 110(a)(2) the directors in attendance constitute a quorum` `directors in attendance` `the greater number`
    WHERE
        `the greater number` MEANS IF `the emergency bylaws fix a greater number` THEN JUST `that greater number` ELSE NOTHING

@export Am I deemed a director at the emergency meeting because I am on the list the board approved (s 110(a)(3))?
GIVEN `I am on the list the board approved before the emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or other person designated on a list approved by the board before the emergency?
      `my turn has come under the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your turn come in the order of priority, and are the conditions in the emergency bylaws or the resolution approving the list met?
      `the period has not run out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period still within what is reasonably necessary after the emergency ended (or is the emergency still on)?
      `my deeming is needed for a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your being deemed a director required to provide a quorum at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed a director at the emergency meeting because I am on the list` IF
    `s 110(a)(3) the person is deemed a director for the meeting` `I am on the list the board approved before the emergency` `my turn has come under the list` `the period has not run out` `my deeming is needed for a quorum`

-- s 110(b), (c)
@export May the board provide lines of succession for the officers at this time (s 110(b))?
GIVEN `the time` IS A `s 110(b) Time of the board's action` @desc When? (Before the emergency; during the emergency; or after the emergency.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board provide lines of succession for the officers at this time` IS
    `s 110(b) the board of directors may provide, and from time to time modify, lines of succession` `the time`

@export May the board change the head office or designate alternative offices at this time (s 110(c))?
GIVEN `the time` IS A `s 110(b) Time of the board's action` @desc When? (Before the emergency; during the emergency; or after the emergency.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board change the head office or designate alternative offices at this time` IS
    `s 110(c) the board of directors may, effective in the emergency, change the head office or designate alternative head offices or regional offices, or authorize the officers to do so` `the time`

-- s 110(d). Protection of the officer, director or employee acting under emergency bylaws.
@export Am I protected from liability for acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws (s 110(d))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS AN Actor @desc Who are you? (An officer; a director; an employee; or someone else.)
      `I acted in accordance with the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in accordance with the emergency bylaws?
      `it was wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your conduct wilful misconduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I protected from liability for acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` IS
    `s 110(d) the person is protected from liability` `who I am` `I acted in accordance with the emergency bylaws` `it was wilful misconduct`

@export Do the bylaws of the corporation stay in effect during the emergency (s 110(e))?
GIVEN `the bylaw conflicts with the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the bylaw inconsistent with the emergency bylaws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this bylaw of the corporation stay in effect during the emergency` IF
    `s 110(e) the bylaw of the corporation remains in effect during the emergency` `the bylaw conflicts with the emergency bylaws`

-- s 110(f), (g)
@export Is the notice I was given of the emergency meeting of the board enough (s 110(f))?
GIVEN `the emergency bylaws say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the emergency bylaws provide otherwise?
      `notice went to every director it was feasible to reach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to every director it was feasible to reach at the time?
      `by feasible means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it given by means that were feasible at the time (including publication or radio)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice I was given of the emergency meeting of the board enough` IS
    `s 110(f) the notice of the meeting of the board of directors is sufficient` `the emergency bylaws say otherwise` `notice went to every director it was feasible to reach` `by feasible means`

@export As an officer present at an emergency board meeting, am I deemed a director (s 110(g))?
GIVEN `the emergency bylaws say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the emergency bylaws provide otherwise?
      `my place in the order of rank and seniority` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting the officers present in order of rank and, within the same rank, seniority, what is your place? (1 for the first.)
      `directors lacking for a quorum` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are lacking to constitute a quorum?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As an officer present at an emergency board meeting, am I deemed a director` IF
    `s 110(g) the officer present is deemed a director for the meeting` `the emergency bylaws say otherwise` `my place in the order of rank and seniority` `directors lacking for a quorum`

-- s 110(i)
@export May the board act on the stockholders' meeting during an emergency condition (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the emergency` IS A `s 110(a) Emergency` @desc What is the emergency condition?
      `a quorum can readily be convened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a quorum of the board be readily convened for a meeting?
      `the board acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board of directors act?
      `a majority of the directors present acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a majority of the directors present act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board act on the stockholders' meeting during an emergency condition` IF
    `s 110(i) the action with respect to the meeting of stockholders is authorized` `the emergency` `a quorum can readily be convened` `the board acted` `a majority of the directors present acted`

@export Which record date applies to the postponed stockholders' meeting (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the record date fixed before the postponement` IS A DATE @desc What record date had been fixed for the meeting before it was postponed?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Which record date applies to the postponed stockholders' meeting` IS
    `s 110(i)(i)(1) the record date that applies to the postponed meeting` `the record date fixed before the postponement`

@export May the corporation tell stockholders of the postponement solely by a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a reporting company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation subject to the reporting requirements of section 13(a) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation tell stockholders solely by a filing with the SEC` IF
    `s 110(i)(i)(2) the corporation may give the notice solely by a document publicly filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission` `the corporation is a reporting company`

@export May the board move the record date and payment date of a declared dividend later (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the record date has not yet occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the record date for the declared dividend not yet occurred?
      `the original record date` IS A DATE @desc What was the original record date?
      `the original payment date` IS A DATE @desc What was the original payment date?
      `the new record date` IS A DATE @desc What is the proposed new record date?
      `the new payment date` IS A DATE @desc What is the proposed new payment date?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board move the record date and payment date of a declared dividend later` IF
    `s 110(i)(ii) the board of directors may change the record date and the payment date of the declared dividend as it has` `the record date has not yet occurred` `the original record date` `the original payment date` `the new record date` `the new payment date`

@export Has the corporation given notice of the change in time (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the day notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation give notice of the change to stockholders?
      `the old record date` IS A DATE @desc What was the record date theretofore in effect?
      `as promptly as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given as promptly as practicable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation given notice of the change in time` IF
    `s 110(i) the corporation has given notice of the change in time` `the day notice was given` `the old record date` `as promptly as practicable`

@export Am I, or the corporation, excused for failing to make the stocklist available during an emergency condition (s 110(i))?
GIVEN `the emergency` IS A `s 110(a) Emergency` @desc What is the emergency condition?
      `inspection was not practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it not practicable to allow inspection of the stocklist during the emergency condition?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, or the corporation, excused for failing to make the stocklist available during an emergency` IF
    `s 110(i) the failure to make a stocklist available is excused` `the emergency` `inspection was not practicable`

§§ `Going to the Court of Chancery (section 111)`

@export May I bring my civil action about this instrument or provision in the Court of Chancery (s 111(a))?
GIVEN `the subject` IS A `s 111(a) Subject of the action` @desc What is the action about? (The certificate or bylaws; an instrument creating or selling stock; an agreement between the corporation and holders of its stock; an agreement to sell, lease or exchange assets with stockholder approval; transfer restrictions under section 202; a proxy; a voting trust or agreement; a merger or consolidation instrument; a conversion certificate; a domestication, transfer or continuance certificate; another instrument the title requires; or none of those.)
      `another court or agency has exclusive jurisdiction by statute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a statute confer exclusive jurisdiction over it on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring my civil action about this instrument or provision in the Court of Chancery` IS
    `s 111(a) the civil action may be brought in the Court of Chancery` `the subject` `another court or agency has exclusive jurisdiction by statute`

@export May I bring my civil action to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of the Delaware General Corporation Law in the Court of Chancery (s 111(b))?
GIVEN `my action is to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of Title 8?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I bring my action to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of the Law in the Court of Chancery` IS
    `s 111(b) the civil action may be brought in the Court of Chancery` `my action is to interpret, apply or enforce a provision of the title`

§§ `Proxy access and proxy expense reimbursement (sections 112 and 113)`

@export Can I, as a stockholder, require the corporation to include my nominee in its proxy solicitation materials (s 112)?
GIVEN `the bylaws provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the bylaws provide that the corporation may be required to include in its proxy materials individuals nominated by a stockholder?
      `the corporation solicits proxies for a director election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation soliciting proxies with respect to an election of directors?
      `I have met the bylaws' conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you met the procedures and conditions the bylaws provide?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I require the corporation to include my nominee in its proxy solicitation materials` IF
    `s 112 the corporation may be required to include the stockholder's nominee in its proxy solicitation materials` `the bylaws provide for it` `the corporation solicits proxies for a director election` `I have met the bylaws' conditions`

@export May the bylaws impose this condition on a stockholder who nominates a director (s 112)?
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `s 112 Condition of access` @desc What is the condition? (A minimum ownership or duration of ownership; submission of specified information; a limit by the number or proportion of nominees or earlier attempts; preclusion for a person who acquired or proposed to acquire a specified percentage of the voting power; an undertaking to indemnify the corporation; or any other condition.)
      `the condition is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For "any other condition": is it lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the bylaws impose this condition on a stockholder who nominates a director` IF
    `s 112 the bylaws may impose the condition` `the condition` `the condition is lawful`

@export Can I, as a stockholder, require the corporation to reimburse the expenses of my proxy solicitation (s 113(a))?
GIVEN `the bylaws provide for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the bylaws provide for reimbursement by the corporation of a stockholder's expenses in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors?
      `my expenses were for soliciting proxies in a director election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the expenses incurred by you in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors?
      `I have met the bylaws' conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you met the procedures and conditions the bylaws prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I require the corporation to reimburse the expenses of my proxy solicitation` IF
    `s 113(a) the corporation may be required to reimburse the stockholder's expenses` `the bylaws provide for it` `my expenses were for soliciting proxies in a director election` `I have met the bylaws' conditions`

@export May the bylaws prescribe this condition for reimbursement of a stockholder's proxy expenses (s 113(a))?
GIVEN `the condition` IS A `s 113(a) Condition of reimbursement` @desc What is the condition? (Eligibility by the number or proportion of nominees or earlier reimbursement; a limit on the amount by the proportion of votes cast or the amount the corporation spent; a limit concerning cumulative voting under section 214; or any other condition.)
      `the condition is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For "any other condition": is it lawful?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the bylaws prescribe this condition for reimbursement` IF
    `s 113(a) the bylaws may prescribe the condition` `the condition` `the condition is lawful`

@export Does the reimbursement bylaw apply to this election (s 113(b))?
GIVEN `the earliest record date for the election` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest record date for the election?
      `the day the bylaw was adopted` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the bylaw adopted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the reimbursement bylaw apply to this election` IF
    `s 113(b) the bylaw applies to the election` `the earliest record date for the election` `the day the bylaw was adopted`

§§ `Nonstock corporations (section 114) -- arises only if the corporation is, or may be, a nonstock corporation`

@export What kind of corporation is mine under section 114(d)?
GIVEN `it is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
      `it is authorized to issue capital stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it authorized to issue capital stock?
      `it has membership interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do its members have membership interests (a share of the profits and losses, or a right to receive distributions of its assets, or both, unless the certificate provides otherwise)?
      `it is exempt under section 501(c)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it exempt from taxation under section 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code (or any successor provisions)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Kind of corporation`
DECIDE `Under section 114(d), what kind of corporation is mine` IS
    `s 114(d) the kind of the corporation` `it is organized under this chapter` `it is authorized to issue capital stock` `it has membership interests` `it is exempt under section 501(c)(3)`

@export Does a member's interest count as a membership interest (s 114(d)(2))?
GIVEN `the certificate provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the nonstock corporation's certificate of incorporation provide otherwise?
      `it is a share of profits and losses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest the member's share of the profits and losses of the nonstock corporation?
      `it is a right to distributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the interest the member's right to receive distributions of the nonstock corporation's assets?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a member's interest count as a membership interest` IF
    `s 114(d)(2) the interest of the member is a membership interest` `the certificate provides otherwise` `it is a share of profits and losses` `it is a right to distributions`

@export In this section, is a reference to stockholders, the board, directors or stock read differently for my nonstock corporation (s 114(a))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Delaware General Corporation Law are you reading? (For example 220.)
      `the part of the section` IS A STRING @desc Which part, written as the lists in section 114(b) and (c) write it, for example (a)(4) or (b)? (Empty if the whole section.)
      `the kind of reference` IS A `s 114(a) Kind of reference` @desc What does the reference say? (Stockholders; the board of directors; directors or members of the board; or stock, capital stock or shares.)
GIVETH A `s 114(a) Reading`
DECIDE `In this section, how is a reference read for my nonstock corporation` IS
    `s 114(a) how the reference in the provision is read` `my kind of corporation` `the provision` `the kind of reference`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS `s 114 Provision` WITH
            section IS `the section number`
            subdivision IS `the part of the section`

@export Does section 114(a)'s reading not apply to this provision, for my kind of corporation (s 114(b), (c))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it?
      `the section number` IS A NUMBER @desc Which section of the Delaware General Corporation Law are you reading? (For example 220.)
      `the part of the section` IS A STRING @desc Which part, written as the lists in section 114(b) and (c) write it, for example (a)(4) or (b)? (Empty if the whole section.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 114(a)'s reading not apply to this provision` IF
    `s 114(b) and (c) subsection (a) does not apply to the provision` `my kind of corporation` `the provision`
    WHERE
        `the provision` MEANS `s 114 Provision` WITH
            section IS `the section number`
            subdivision IS `the part of the section`

@export Is my corporation a nonstock corporation (s 114(d)(4))?
GIVEN `it is organized under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation organized under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
      `it is authorized to issue capital stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it authorized to issue capital stock?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation a nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 114(d)(4) the corporation is a nonstock corporation` `it is organized under this chapter` `it is authorized to issue capital stock`

@export Is my nonstock corporation a nonprofit nonstock corporation (s 114(d)(3))?
GIVEN `it is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a nonstock corporation?
      `it has membership interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have membership interests?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nonstock corporation a nonprofit nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 114(d)(3) the corporation is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `it is a nonstock corporation` `it has membership interests`

@export Is my nonprofit nonstock corporation a charitable nonstock corporation (s 114(d)(1))?
GIVEN `it is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a nonprofit nonstock corporation?
      `it is exempt under section 501(c)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it exempt from taxation under section 501(c)(3) of the United States Internal Revenue Code (or any successor provisions)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nonprofit nonstock corporation a charitable nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 114(d)(1) the corporation is a charitable nonstock corporation` `it is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `it is exempt under section 501(c)(3)`

§§ `Forum selection (section 115)`

@export Is my claim an internal corporate claim (s 115(b))?
GIVEN `it is based on a violation of a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim (including a claim in the right of the corporation) based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director, officer or stockholder in that capacity?
      `section 111 lets it be brought in Chancery` IS A `s 111(a) Subject of the action` @desc What is the claim about? (The kinds section 111(a) lists, or none of those.)
      `a statute gives another tribunal exclusive jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a statute confer exclusive jurisdiction over it on a court, agency or tribunal other than the Court of Chancery?
      `another section gives Chancery jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a section of Title 8 other than section 111 confer jurisdiction on the Court of Chancery over the claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim an internal corporate claim` IF
    `s 115(b) the claim is an internal corporate claim` `it is based on a violation of a duty` `Chancery has jurisdiction under the title`
    WHERE
        `Chancery has jurisdiction under the title` MEANS
            `s 115(b)(ii) this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` (`s 111(a) the civil action may be brought in the Court of Chancery` `section 111 lets it be brought in Chancery` `a statute gives another tribunal exclusive jurisdiction`) `another section gives Chancery jurisdiction`

@export Can the certificate or bylaws force me to bring an internal corporate claim only in Delaware courts, and can they stop me bringing it there (s 115(a))?
GIVEN `the provision requires Delaware courts only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision require that internal corporate claims be brought solely and exclusively in any or all of the courts in this State?
      `the provision prohibits bringing them in Delaware courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision prohibit bringing internal corporate claims in the courts of this State?
      `it is consistent with the jurisdictional requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this forum provision for internal corporate claims permitted` IS
    `s 115(a) the provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws is permitted` `the provision requires Delaware courts only` `the provision prohibits bringing them in Delaware courts` `it is consistent with the jurisdictional requirements`

@export Can the certificate or bylaws force me, as a stockholder, to bring a claim that is not an internal corporate claim only in a prescribed forum (s 115(c))?
GIVEN `my claim is an internal corporate claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim an internal corporate claim?
      `I bring it as a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you bringing it in your capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation?
      `it relates to the corporation's business or affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or the rights or powers of the corporation or its stockholders, directors or officers?
      `it is consistent with the jurisdictional requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement consistent with applicable jurisdictional requirements?
      `it leaves me one Delaware court with jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requirement allow you to bring the claim in at least one court in this State that has jurisdiction over it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the certificate or bylaws force me to bring a claim only in a prescribed forum` IS
    `s 115(c) the certificate or the bylaws may require the stockholder to bring the claim only in the prescribed forums` `my claim is an internal corporate claim` `I bring it as a stockholder` `it relates to the corporation's business or affairs` `it is consistent with the jurisdictional requirements` `it leaves me one Delaware court with jurisdiction`

§§ `Documents, signatures and delivery (section 116)`

@export Is this a document, and is an electronic transmission the equivalent of a written document (s 116(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the medium` IS A `s 116(a)(1) Medium` @desc What is it? (A tangible medium on which information is inscribed; an electronic transmission; or another medium.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(1), is this a document` IF
    `s 116(a)(1) the medium is a document` `the medium`

@export Is an electronic transmission deemed the equivalent of a written document (s 116(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the medium` IS A `s 116(a)(1) Medium` @desc What is it? (A tangible medium on which information is inscribed; an electronic transmission; or another medium.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(1), is this deemed the equivalent of a written document` IF
    `s 116(a)(1) the medium is deemed the equivalent of a written document` `the medium`

@export May I sign in this form where the Law, the certificate or the bylaws require or permit a signature (s 116(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the form` IS A `s 116(a)(2) Form of signature` @desc What form is the signature? (Manual; facsimile; conformed; electronic; or another form.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(2), may I sign in this form` IS
    `s 116(a)(2) the form of signature may be used` `the form`

@export Is my symbol or process an electronic signature (s 116(a)(2))?
GIVEN `it is electronic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an electronic symbol or process?
      `it is attached to or associated with the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it attached to, or logically associated with, the document?
      `I executed or adopted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it executed or adopted by you?
      `I meant to execute, authenticate or adopt the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do so with an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(2), is my symbol or process an electronic signature` IF
    `s 116(a)(2) the symbol or process is an electronic signature` `it is electronic` `it is attached to or associated with the document` `I executed or adopted it` `I meant to execute, authenticate or adopt the document`

@export Is my electronic transmission deemed delivered to the recipient (s 116(a)(3))?
GIVEN `we agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the sender and the recipient agreed otherwise?
      `it entered the recipient's designated system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it entered an information processing system that the recipient has designated for receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered?
      `it is in a form the system can process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in a form capable of being processed by that system?
      `the recipient can retrieve it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the recipient able to retrieve it?
      `it is a stockholder's proxy or consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a proxy or consent given by or on behalf of a stockholder?
      `the extra requirements for proxies and consents are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the additional requirements of section 212(c)(2) and (3), or section 228(d)(1), met?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(3), is my electronic transmission deemed delivered to the recipient` IS
    `s 116(a)(3) the electronic transmission is deemed delivered to the person` `we agreed otherwise` `it entered the recipient's designated system` `it is in a form the system can process` `the recipient can retrieve it` `it is a stockholder's proxy or consent` `the extra requirements for proxies and consents are met`

@export Has the recipient designated this information processing system (s 116(a)(3))?
GIVEN `the certificate or bylaws show it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws show that the recipient designated the system?
      `the circumstances show it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the context and surrounding circumstances, including the parties' conduct, show that the recipient designated the system?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under section 116(a)(3), has the recipient designated this information processing system` IF
    `s 116(a)(3) the person has designated the information processing system` `the certificate or bylaws show it` `the circumstances show it`

@export Does delivery of an electronic transmission to me depend on anyone's being aware of its receipt (s 116(a)(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does delivery of an electronic transmission depend on anyone's being aware of its receipt` IF
    `s 116(a)(3) delivery requires that a person be aware of the receipt`

@export Does an electronic acknowledgement prove that the transmission was received, and that its content is what was sent (s 116(a)(3))?
GIVEN `I received an electronic acknowledgement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an electronic acknowledgement received from the information processing system?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic acknowledgement prove that the transmission was received` IF
    `s 116(a)(3) the electronic acknowledgement establishes that the electronic transmission was received` `I received an electronic acknowledgement`

@export Does an electronic acknowledgement by itself prove that the content received is the content sent (s 116(a)(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an electronic acknowledgement by itself prove that the content received is the content sent` IF
    `s 116(a)(3) the electronic acknowledgement by itself establishes that the content sent corresponds to the content received`

@export May we conduct this transaction in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6 (s 116(a))?
GIVEN `the parts governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered as it requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the parts of the transaction governed by the Delaware General Corporation Law documented, signed and delivered in accordance with section 116(a) or otherwise in accordance with the Law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we conduct this transaction in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6` IF
    `s 116(a) this chapter does not prohibit conducting the transaction in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6` `the parts governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered as it requires`

@export Do the electronic document and signature rules of section 116(a) apply to this document (s 116(b))?
GIVEN `the kind of document` IS A `s 116(b) Kind of document` @desc What is it? (A document filed with or submitted to the Secretary of State, the Register in Chancery, a court or other body; part of the stock ledger; a certificate representing a security; a notice or waiver of notice; a ballot; an act under section 280 or subchapter III, XIII or XVI; or any other document.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the electronic document and signature rules apply to this document` IF
    `s 116(b) subsection (a) applies to the document` `the kind of document`

@export Can the certificate or bylaws limit my use of electronic transmission or signature (s 116(b))?
GIVEN `the provision restricts electronic means expressly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the provision expressly restrict or prohibit the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature (or any form of them)?
      `the provision restricts delivery to a system expressly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it expressly restrict or prohibit the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing system?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the provision of the certificate or bylaws limit the application of section 116(a)` IF
    `s 116(b) the provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws limits the application of subsection (a)` `the provision restricts electronic means expressly` `the provision restricts delivery to a system expressly`

@export Does a rule that excludes a document from section 116(a) create a presumption about how to document, sign or deliver it (s 116(b))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the exclusion create a presumption about the lawful means to document, sign or deliver` IF
    `s 116(b) a presumption arises from the exclusions about the lawful means to document, sign or deliver`

@export Does the Delaware General Corporation Law control over the federal Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act (s 116(c))?
GIVEN `a provision of the Law is deemed to modify that Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a provision of the Delaware General Corporation Law deemed to modify, limit or supersede the Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act?
      `section 7002(a)(2) of that Act permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 7002(a)(2) of that Act permit the chapter to control?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Delaware General Corporation Law control over the federal Act` IS
    `s 116(c) this chapter controls` `a provision of the Law is deemed to modify that Act` `section 7002(a)(2) of that Act permits it`
